 "text": "Hey! How's everything going? It depends how much you ride. If you do a few hundred miles a year, a simple pressure gauge and filling it up once a month is probably enough. Inflate it to the chosen pressure while someone else holds the hose. Then note the pressure gauge reading and double it to plan ahead. That's it. Going too high can damage the tube between the rims. Yes, a few PSI less than normal helps the sealant do its magic without being too soft.",
